#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff2f1a9d-2b0e-5a18-98d5-4f49f6f1527b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating an Integral Given Another Integral With Reversed Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "703ed312-09c5-5253-91b6-f0d434be889d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371489} {:answer/id #uuid "1fa56dd7-6869-5784-aa0a-edc637661c42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fa56dd7-6869-5784-aa0a-edc637661c42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371490} :answer-field/id #uuid "f25acaa6-6b20-51a5-8263-75f78e25820b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f9f00b1-7b9d-5c2d-924d-2b87fbdf35be" :question/math-academy-id "q-346043" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5(-4)\\,+\\,x\\,{|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =-20\\,+\\,(6-0) \\\\  & =-20\\,+\\,6 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff2f1a9d-2b0e-5a18-98d5-4f49f6f1527b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating an Integral Given Another Integral With Reversed Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e15b143b-eafb-5b87-a8dc-4a16ec1aa25e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287246} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf86f9e-790d-5745-857c-1df6f91fc584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e15b143b-eafb-5b87-a8dc-4a16ec1aa25e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287246} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad9497f7-a6bd-57c1-aaf5-1c8b8e0f4b4a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287245}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "246ea688-360e-5196-a83d-e47bea5b22da" :question/math-academy-id "q-346057" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3,$ calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(3)\\,+\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{16-1}{2} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Definite Integral Given Integrals Over Adjacent Intervals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78fd6ee6-5862-5ba8-a58d-cb3096d027a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371493} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c742a4-d2a2-5ce3-ba0a-4aecf4d8b2db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9c742a4-d2a2-5ce3-ba0a-4aecf4d8b2db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371494} :answer-field/id #uuid "96e52d5e-ec5b-5638-bfa7-eefc112d12f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f83467c-530c-58f9-8cd1-4868e8f44e12" :question/math-academy-id "q-346195" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0$ and ${\\int }_{7}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5,$ then what is ${\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{7}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n0+5\\,=\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,4{\\int }_{3}^{10}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(5)\\,-\\,4\\cdot x{|}_{3}^{10} \\\\  & =15\\,-\\,4(10-3) \\\\  & =15-28 \\\\  & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Definite Integral Using Multiple Properties of Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010f6d81-ea51-5c35-afe3-92e501cf4cba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "010f6d81-ea51-5c35-afe3-92e501cf4cba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371497} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bc84e42-6427-5f88-b8fb-ad51dd36c9c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf40ca30-e264-5872-9e23-27d42025a110" :question/math-academy-id "q-346219" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{5}^{-1}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=14$ and ${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{-1}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ 7{\\int }_{5}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ -7{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ {\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Definite Integral Using Multiple Properties of Definite Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9af75731-9d6b-570c-9e38-da632e4e2cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371500} {:answer/id #uuid "2f527ab2-4d47-509b-afc6-2fde0d5098ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371501} {:answer/id #uuid "b9841610-e997-56ce-8484-1b4a01980e43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371502} {:answer/id #uuid "29301357-5df5-5dcf-9709-c9366689d721" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371503} {:answer/id #uuid "7259ccf7-26b5-5f6c-bf79-d8e5b0f3e584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f527ab2-4d47-509b-afc6-2fde0d5098ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371501} :answer-field/id #uuid "d41272b3-dba2-5744-a3aa-ead96b62928c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e557d0aa-f53c-521a-8a1c-fd93dd8bf83a" :question/math-academy-id "q-4797" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{2}^{-2}\\frac{1}{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3$ and ${\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=10.$  What is the value of ${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}\\frac{1}{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12+10 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
